 \u2014 a rushing-yards spot.</p><p>Efficiency edge to LA \u2014 a 49% success-rate offense against a NYG defense that allows 46% \u2014 points should come.</p><p><strong>Jaxson Dart</strong> has a passing-yards tailwind \u2014 LA allow <strong>239 pass yds/game</strong> (vs ~230).</p><p><strong>Malik Nabers</strong> draws a plus matchup \u2014 LA concede <strong>68 yds/game to WR1s</strong> (league ~58), and NYG funnel 29% of targets his way. A rec-yards spot.</p><p><strong>Isaiah Likely</strong> has room to work \u2014 LA allow <strong>41 yds/game to TE1s</strong> (vs ~35), a receiving-yards and target angle.</p><p><strong>Cam Skattebo</strong> eats as a receiver too \u2014 LA give up 23 rec yds/game to backs, and NYG target the RB on 18% of throws.</p><h3>Touchdown Board</h3><p><strong>Kyren Williams</strong> is a bell-cow (68% of carries) meeting a defense that allows 0.53 RB rushing TDs/game \u2014 strong anytime-TD equity.</p><p><strong>Malik Nabers</strong> carries TD equity \u2014 LA surrender 0.59 WR1 receiving scores a game.</p><h3>Game Script, Pace & Environment</h3><p>Fade the NYG run \u2014 as 10-point dogs projected to chase, <strong>Cam Skattebo</strong>'s carries get squeezed, though his receiving work ticks up in catch-up mode.</p><p>A middling 48 total \u2014 no strong lean either way; the value is in the individual matchups above, not the game environment.</p><p><strong>Indoors</strong> \u2014 a dome removes weather variance and historically nudges passing efficiency up; a small tailwind for the passing games.</p><h3>LA \u2014 a <em>balanced</em> offense</h3><p>LA are a balanced offense \u2014 their run/pass split by game state tracks the league closely (44% pass when leading vs 44% average), so their players' usage is driven more by role than by any strong situational lean.</p><p><strong>Kyren Williams</strong> (13 carries, 57 yards projected) gets a mild game-script tailwind as a favorite, though LA's willingness to keep throwing when ahead caps